WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.079
Building a batch pipeline for 200 product photos.

2
00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:10.280
A real walk through of the Workspace: resize, watermark, strip metadata,

3
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.197
convert and zip, then save it as a recipe you can run again.

4
00:00:16.692 --> 00:00:19.849
Plan the steps. I start by writing the steps down in order.

5
00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:26.596
Build it in the Workspace. Open the Workspace, drop the folder of photos,

6
00:00:26.596 --> 00:00:29.219
and add the steps from the list on the left.

7
00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:36.222
Save it as a recipe. Once it looks right, save the pipeline as a recipe.

8
00:00:38.616 --> 00:00:40.600
Why it is fast. There is no upload.

9
00:00:42.995 --> 00:00:45.910
To try it, open Image Resizer in OpenFile.

10
00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.866
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

11
00:00:49.866 --> 00:00:53.405
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

12
00:00:56.095 --> 00:00:59.700
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
